 "critic": "The clearest families are paid errands, isolated wrongs, assault-driven help, duty-breaking discovery, and help that turns into a reckoning. Most traces omit concrete motives, requested acts and consequences; naming participants or declaring an outcome resolved does not supply those links. Requests to act against the asker are especially hard to interpret. The paid jobs offer useful objectives and plausible local concerns, but instant completion hides both the action and its payoff. Repeated structures with substituted names weaken individuality, while Night City often comes through only in gang references, eddies and a few locations. Explicit declines provide clearer resting points than unexplained closing labels."
